Package: tandem
Version: 3.6
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), zenity, desktop-file-utils, xdg-utils, unzip, libglib2.0-bin
Recommends: libnotify-bin, wine, winetricks, waydroid, adb, curl | wget
Maintainer: Paulo Eduardo <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ChrnX0/Tandem
Description: Run Windows programs and Android apps by double-clicking
 Tandem makes .exe, .msi, .apk and .xapk files behave like native
 applications on Linux. Double-click a file and it runs.
 .
 For Windows programs it detects missing runtime libraries from Wine's
 own error output, maps them to winetricks packages, installs them and
 retries - the loop an experienced user would do by hand.
 .
 For Android apps it inspects the package before installing: ABI,
 minimum SDK and split-package layout, so incompatibilities are
 reported in plain language instead of failing silently. Split
 packages (.xapk/.apks/.apkm) are installed through ADB.
 .
 Wine prefixes that Tandem did not create are treated as read-only,
 so production systems are never modified by the automation.
